":81.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.1553111838132613,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":69.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.013983583101737659,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":-0.07486974755271844,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.3433480072890873,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.06802685943983192,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":10.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.02132919903734598,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":14.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.08928419220298944,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.005485518015783108,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":44.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.03519889081004817,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":35.2,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03219715914774433,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":46.9,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.07826585887188242,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.005024843027532577,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.14067,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":93.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Genesco Inc. operates as a retailer and wholesaler of footwear, apparel, and accessories. The company operates through four segments: Journeys Group, Schuh Group, Johnston & Murphy Group, and Genesco Brands Group. The Journeys Group segment offers footwear and accessories for young men, women, and children through the Journeys, Journeys Kidz, and Little Burgundy retail chains, as well as through e-commerce operations. The Schuh Group segment operates Schuh retail footwear stores that offer casual and athletic footwear, as well as sells footwear through e-commerce. The Johnston & Murphy Group segment is involved in the retail and e-commerce operations; and wholesale distribution of footwear, apparel, and accessories primarily for men. The Genesco Brands Group segment markets footwear under the Levi's, Dockers, and other brands. The company provides its products through catalogs and e-commerce websites, including journeys.com, journeyskidz.com, journeys.ca, schuh.co.uk, schuh.ie, schuh.eu, littleburgundyshoes.com, johnstonmurphy.com, and nashvilleshoewarehouse.com. It operates retail stores in the United States, Puerto Rico, Canada, the United Kingdom, and the Republic of Ireland primarily under the Journeys, Journeys Kidz, Schuh, Little Burgundy, and Johnston & Murphy brands. Genesco Inc. was incorporated in 1934 and is headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Mimi Eckel Vaughn | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $508K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Genesco Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $390M market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and -2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 48%.","The business throws off $84M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 10.99\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -9.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): roic below cost of capital; structural revenue/margin decline \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Technical Reactions to GCO Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/Technical_Reactions_to_GCO_Trends_in_Macro_Strategies_103026045401_1793350441.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793350441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Deckers Rides International Strength as HOKA & UGG Demand Holds Firm","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/deckers-rides-international-strength-hoka-153800223.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793720280.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.868,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Capri Holdings Strengthens Brand Appeal Through Deeper Consumer Ties","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3021398/capri-holdings-strengthens-brand-appeal-through-deeper-consumer-ties?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Crank_focused-3021398","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793704740.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CPRI Q2 Earnings Beat on Jimmy Choo Growth, FY'27 Outlook Raised","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3020618/cpri-q2-earnings-beat-on-jimmy-choo-growth-fy-27-outlook-raised?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_article-3020618","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793627940.0,"origin":"t